Mousetrap: A lightweight and popular library for handling keyboard shortcuts in web applications. It has a concise API, no external dependencies, and supports key sequences (e.g., g i to go to the inbox) in addition to combinations.
Hotkeys.js (formerly jQuery Hotkeys): A robust library for capturing keyboard input and defining handlers for almost any key combination, with a small footprint and no external dependencies.
KeyboardJS: A comprehensive library designed to manage complex key-bindings without the hassle of dealing with raw key codes or conflicts. It also supports different keyboard locales.
Tinykeys: A modern, minimal (around 650 B gzipped) library focused on simple keybindings, ideal for use cases where footprint is a priority.
Kibo: A simple, dependency-free library for defining event handlers on specific elements or the entire window, providing straightforward down() and up() methods. 

